## 23-Nov-7:50pm-PST — Muse: the trajectories bound corrected to a fixed horizontal line for the running maximum

ChatGPT's signed email of 7:24 PM this evening, item 7 of its proof progress review, found a mathematical mismatch in the trajectories chart I redrew an hour earlier, and it was right. The panel defines its precise object as M(N), the running maximum over satisfiable formulas F with |F| <= N of L(F) / log2(|F| + 2), for the efficient interpreter the proofs state. The chart plotted the per formula envelope a + c / log2(n + 2) as an upper bound for that maximum, and that does not follow: a per formula bound L(F) <= a log2(|F| + 2) + c bounds each formula's normalized cost at its own length, but the maximum at N can be attained by a smaller formula, whose normalized value stays in the running maximum while the plotted envelope declines.

**The fix.** The bound for M(N) now stands as a fixed horizontal line, A = a + max(c, 0). Since log2(|F| + 2) >= 1 for every F, each formula's normalized cost stays at or under a + max(c, 0), so M(N) stays at or under A at every N; and a bounded running maximum in turn supplies a uniform normalized constant directly. I redrew the main panel of assets/security-tokens-trajectories-2026-11-23.svg: the descending dotted curve and its settling line are gone, and 1 dotted horizontal line stands in their place. The legend strip entry now reads as the fixed bound for the running maximum, A = a + max(c, 0), horizontal, conditional, not a result, still keyed by its dotted white swatch, with no text on any line. The same correction stands in the treatment at the bottom of the statistics page and in candidate B on the candidates page, in the image descriptions on those pages and in the README, and in a note in the candidates page head recording the find. The underlying equivalence is unchanged: the running maximum is bounded if and only if P = NP and tends to infinity if and only if P != NP, conditional on the efficiently simulated universal interpreter already specified. The fates stay dashed and schematic, the finite checks stay off the axes, and the frontier on candidate C stays hypothetical.

**One wording alignment.** The conductor's own README edit of 7:42 PM moved the Mirrors and links section to the very bottom, so the chart section now stands second from the bottom. I rebased this landing over his edit, preserved his section order exactly, and the prose in the README chart section, the statistics treatment and the candidates page now says the chart stands near the bottom of the README.

**The render check.** I rendered the redrawn chart to an image at its full 900 pixel width with cairosvg and inspected it panel by panel. The dotted bound runs clean and horizontal across the main panel; the amber bounded fate settles under it; the teal escaping fate crosses it and leaves the top right, as an escaping fate should; the header lines sit in clear space; the legend strip reads in full with no line through any word. The hinge, theorem and evidence panels are unchanged and clean, and the footer lines stand inside the canvas.

**The tests.** The figure slot, link resolution and reader quiet batch passes at 58 tests, and the wider doc batch (default divergences, feature tiers, version rot, design docs, personal docs, the cs office doc and the gmail discipline doc, with the same 3 modules) passes at 1036 tests, on the tree this landed on; the quick batch passed again after the rebase over the conductor's README edit. The shrink guard is clean, and no new file stands in the repository root.

