## 19-Nov-12:34am-PST — Claude: an additional accessibility workaround, 1 typed letter after a call

Claude, for every seat and agent that works this repository
with the owner, at his word. This adds 1 case to the 5:11 PM
entry of 18-Nov, which sets out the O and V signals. Those
stand as written.

**What is added.** A letter typed after a call asks for both
jobs in the 1 turn, whichever of the 2 letters it is:

1. The seat goes on with the work on the branch in hand, as
   V asks.
2. The seat makes the full sync, as O asks, so the next call
   starts informed.

The typed reply is a short ping and nothing more. It says
the letter arrived and that the seat is ready for the next
call. What was done and what was read is held for that call,
and it stands in the tree, where it can be checked.

**Why it is here.** This is an additional accessibility
workaround, in use from 19-Nov. The owner talks the work
over with this seat on calls. On a call this seat can talk,
and it cannot reach the repository, run anything, or read
what another seat has landed. Nor can it begin work at the
2 moments where that would help most: when a call is picked
up, and when a call is dropped. On this seat's side, work
begins only at a typed line.

So the typed letter stands in for those 2 moments:

- **The drop.** The call ends and the owner types 1 letter.
  The work and the sync are both done in that turn.
- **The pickup.** The next call begins with the state
  already read, so a question about what any seat has done
  is answered from what was read.

**What it costs.** 1 hand-off for each round: the call
ends, a letter is typed, and the next call waits for the
ping. The owner carries that cost. That is why this stands
on the record as a workaround, and not as the way the work
ought to go.

**How it is said.** This is a limit of the tools this seat
is given on a call today, and it is written here as a fact.
There is no blame in it for any house or for any seat. What
has been reported to the people who build this seat's app
is in the 5:11 PM entry, and what passes between the owner
and them is his.

**For any seat.** Nothing here is this seat's own. A seat
whose call side cannot reach the tree can take the same
shape: 1 typed letter after a call, both jobs in the turn,
and a short ping back.

