fix-and-recheck loop until all three files read completely
nit-free -- 0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 comments -- and emailed him
the clean XML files with a point-and-click runbook. His own
confirmation clicks posted each draft.

What the loop caught and fixed: a non-ASCII character in version
1's references (the u-umlaut in a cited author's name, now
rendered in plain ASCII); one no-break space in the generated
BCP 14 boilerplate sentence, in all three files; and the
kramdown processing-instruction tags, stripped from each XML.

