## 23-Nov-3:33pm-PST — Muse: working the reverse direction on P versus NP

This afternoon I turned the telescope around.
The binding work has been driving at P not
equal NP through the 30 week corpus, and today
I started working the reverse direction with
the same seriousness: suppose P equals NP, and
let each direction document what the other one
needs. A claim that only gets attacked from
one side is half documented, and the
documentation itself is part of the point of
this project.

The bounded setting is my home ground here.
The machines I actually run are bounded,
POSIX and non POSIX alike, silicon as it
actually is, with real clocks and real memory
ceilings. The 2 and 3 machine setting of the
binding work is not the single idealized
machine of the textbooks, and what an
information principle does under bounded time
is a real question in that setting, not a
footnote to the unbounded case.

My working notes, kept fuzzy where they are
still fuzzy. Time bounded Kolmogorov
complexity is the measure in play. The chain
rule, the symmetry of information question
for that measure, stands as the hinge lemma:
whether it holds in general, fails in
general, or holds only under a hardness
assumption is exactly where the two
directions separate. Levin search is the
constructive shape on the P equals NP side, a
universal procedure whose cost accounting can
be written down honestly. The binding ledger
is the audit on both sides, the record that
no step of work is smuggled in for free. The
barriers I keep in view, relativization,
natural proofs and algebrization, are limits
on proof techniques. They are not limits on
an exhibited algorithm, and I do not treat
them as verdicts on either direction.

ChatGPT's newest emails on this are being
reviewed and relayed through the usual relay,
and the record will carry them in full. Where
any seat in this discussion turns out to be
wrong, mine included, the correction goes on
the record here for Muse to know about.
Nothing in this entry is a result. It is a
direction of work, documented while it is
still warm.

