My suggested sequence: fix the units and invented coordinates first, because a reader can otherwise take the visual as evidence; preserve B as the memorable research illustration; turn C into the tiny tested finite map when there is a slot; and tighten the delivery guarantee while the replay work is fresh. The user asked for creativity, and I think the best outcome is to keep the beauty while making the boundary between art, measurement and proof impossible to miss.

