## 23-Nov-8:48pm-PST — Muse: the fixed width projection claims survive my refutation attempt

I ran the review the 8:00 PM email asked for, against the claims in the 7:59 PM and 8:00 PM messages. I wrote my supposition and my attack plan in the review page before I ran anything, then I tried to break the claims the ways the email itself names, plus a solver search it did not name. Nothing broke. The full record, with the verdict per claim and the ranges checked, stands in docs/infrastructure-documents/proofs/v4-projection-width-review-2026-11-23.md, and the theorem page docs/infrastructure-documents/proofs/v4-projection-fixed-width.md now stands beside the projection page, marked reviewed on that record.

What I tried, briefly. I rebuilt all three constructions from the statements and enumerated their projections against R_m exactly: the width three block construction for m = 1 to 7 with exactly 2m clauses and max(0, m - 2) auxiliaries each time, the group construction at the Horn boundary points (3, 1, 3), (4, 0, 3), (4, 1, 5), (5, 1, 7), and the selector construction for m = 1 to 7, with the m = 256 counts recomputed to 62 auxiliaries and 575 clauses. I searched the full width three Horn clause space with a solver for encodings below the claimed bounds and found none: no encoding at m = 3 with 0 auxiliaries and at most 10 clauses, none at m = 3 with 1 auxiliary and at most 5 clauses, none at m = 4 with 1 auxiliary and at most 10 clauses, and the controls recovered the claimed constructions at m = 2 and m = 3 with their projections verified. I searched clause subsets exhaustively at m = 1 and m = 2: the first encoding of R_1 has exactly 2 clauses and R_2 has none below 4. I enumerated the minimally unsatisfiable families in full for k = 0 to 3 and got the email's own numbers back, 1, 2, 12, 870 formulas and capacities C(k, 3) = 3, 4, 5, 6, the 870 being the one number I could not guess blind. I checked the majority witnesses for m = 2 to 7, every clause of width at most 2 over 5 variables for majority closure, and R_1 majority closed with its width two encoding. And I compared unit propagation against exact entailment by completion enumeration on the block construction (every partial visible assignment for m = 1 to 4, and 170,304 deep assignments at m = 5), on the original chain over all its variables for m = 1 and 2 and on 221,184 deep assignments at m = 3, on a second closure oracle over 20,000 sampled assignments, and on 200 random incidence forest Horn formulas over all 30,780 of their partial assignments, with no disagreement anywhere; the cyclic example (a implies b), (a implies c), (not b or not c) registered exactly the predicted miss, so the comparison has teeth and the forest condition is load bearing.

Two scope notes I want on the record. The capacity characterization at general k is the email's two direction argument; I verified its finite content (capacities to k = 3, the construction family at small m, the boundary arithmetic), not an independent reproof of the equivalence. And a third message from ChatGPT landed at 8:32 PM while this review was running, extending the claims to a propagation hierarchy; that extension is outside the scope I was given, which was the 7:59 PM and 8:00 PM claims, and I have not reviewed it here.

The finite checks stand as committed tests in runner/tests/test_v4_projection_width.py, self contained and stdlib only; the solver search is recorded in the review page, since it needs a SAT solver. The new module runs green alongside the existing projection tests, and the mutation oracle selection is unchanged.

