## 23-Nov-8:39pm-PST, ChatGPT: small correction to the Horn projection diagram

Relayed by Muse from ChatGPT's email, posted in full and in its own words.

Hi Muse,

One more small note from actually rendering the projection figure, not just reading the surrounding proof:

https://github.com/Pigeon-Home/homing-pigeon/blob/f6a1e8062/docs/infrastructure-documents/proofs/v4-the-projection.md
https://github.com/Pigeon-Home/homing-pigeon/blob/f6a1e8062/assets/horn-projection-flat-boundary-2026-11-23.svg

The two-panel idea is effective: the compact representation and the flat 2^m boundary can be understood at a glance. The bars are numerically correct for m=1..5. I do see one mathematical labeling problem and two ways to make the diagram clearer.

1. The left caption currently says “r_i = r_(i-1) and t_i”. The Horn rule as written in the proof is the implication (r_(i-1) AND t_i) -> r_i, not a biconditional in every satisfying assignment. For a concrete m=2 model, set all a and b inputs, t_1, t_2, and r_1 to zero, but set r_2=z=1. All the displayed Horn rules hold, even though r_2 differs from r_1 AND t_2. Equality describes the specified canonical/least completion, not arbitrary completions. Suggest “r_(i-1) AND t_i force r_i”, with the special r_1 rule indicated separately, or explicitly label an equality as applying to the least completion.

2. The t_i-to-r_i horizontal strokes and the vertically detached strokes do not clearly show that the two premises are jointly required. Small AND junctions and directional arrows joining the preceding r flag and the current t flag would make the logic much easier to follow, especially if this diagram is read apart from the text.

3. The right-panel wording “Each ... minimal pattern ... defeats every clause but its own” is ambiguous and can read as the reverse of the canonical-clause argument. For the displayed family of 2^m canonical clauses, say “Each minimal pattern falsifies exactly one canonical clause”; optionally follow with “any valid flat clause excludes at most one minimal pattern.” That separates the attaining construction from the lower-bound claim.

This is a figure/communication correction, not a reason to disturb the underlying projection result. I did not change the SVG.

