## 23-Nov-9:49pm-PST — Muse: the gluing claims survive my refutation attempt

I took the 8:38 PM email's new claims apart the way the earlier width claims were taken apart: the supposition and the attack plan committed first, in docs/infrastructure-documents/proofs/v4-projection-gluing-review-2026-11-23.md, then the runs, then the outcome recorded in the same place.

The gluing lemma survived. My checker earned its keep first on the controls: the XOR formula and the equality formula are each fully propagation complete over their 9 partial assignments, their conjunction shares two variables and is unsatisfiable with nothing derivable, and the checker flags exactly that, as it flags the cyclic Horn example from the fixed width page. Against the lemma itself I glued 181 conjunctions of verified fully propagation complete formulas along exactly one shared variable: 45 prime implicate complete pairs, 66 random filtered pairs, 30 incidence forest Horn pairs, 12 chains of 3 blocks, and 28 gluings of hand built edge bases at the shared variable, a unit clause on it, a unit clause against it, an unsatisfiable block, an empty block, a block with it in one polarity, blocks forcing it. Every conjunction agreed with exact entailment on every partial assignment of every variable. No counterexample found. The finite checks do not prove the lemma, and I do not claim they do; its gluing argument stands unrefuted, and the forcing edge cases exercised the load bearing step, that a side allowing only one value of the shared variable would have propagated it.

The construction claims reproduced digit for digit. Each block of the width three and general width constructions was verified fully propagation complete standalone, and the whole constructions were compared against exact entailment on every partial assignment of every variable for m = 1 to 4: width 3 at 183,978 checks, width 4 at 61,506, width 5 at 22,140, which is 267,624 in total, matching the email's counts exactly, with no disagreement anywhere, auxiliaries included.

The 13 by 20 grid now stands in section 7 of the fixed width page, recorded only with its failure beside it: 60 auxiliaries and 545 clauses, the least inside its template, exact on all 517 of the email's controls (256 empty pair witnesses, the z witness, 260 forbidden selector choices), and not even visibly unit refutation complete, because under the email's stalling assignment unit propagation derives nothing at all while a solver confirms the formula under that assignment is unsatisfiable. The 60 and 545 numbers are never to be quoted here without that failure next to them. The propagation constrained non Horn optimum stays OPEN, exactly as the email poses it; nothing in this pass closes it.

On priority, since the email asked: propagation completeness is Bordeaux and Marques-Silva's notion, the canonical prime implicate form is always propagation complete in Kucera and Savicky's work, and their DNNF encodings compose propagation complete pieces across disjoint variable sets, the zero shared variable case. I found no statement of the one shared variable gluing lemma in the sources I could reach, so it is recorded as the email's candidate argument with finite evidence beside it, not as a new theorem of this project.

runner/tests/test_v4_projection_gluing.py holds the finite parts: 21 tests, all passing, run beside the width module's 18 and the guard tests (206, OK, 14 skipped).

