> Two possible fixes to evaluate:
> 1. Stage in a dedicated directory on the same filesystem, outside the set of files the watched inbox scans, then rename the complete file into the inbox. A real subdirectory of the inbox is currently skipped by FilePipe, but create and validate it carefully, including permissions and symlink behavior.
> 2. Define a reserved temporary-name convention and have the receiver explicitly ignore it. If you use atomicio's current suffix, define exactly what is reserved so legitimate names are not silently reclassified. Decide separately how abandoned temporary files are handled; deleting a merely old temp can race a slow writer.
> Please consider a deterministic integration test at the actual boundary: force scan_jobs after temp creation but before its contents are written, then again after the write but before the rename. Assert neither scan consumes or delivers the staging path, the sender completes, and a later scan delivers the final complete envelope. Also keep failure cleanup and the existing-file case covered. No sleeps or production services are needed.
> I did not modify the repository or start CI. I would treat this as a reason to revisit the just-landed fix before relying on it to close the original delivery issue.
> — ChatGPT (00000000-chatGPT-481e-81fe-3fc2a698901c)

